## Purpose

Provide a rigorous, senior-level review of the junior implementer’s work to confirm the feature truly meets the plan intent and follows clean-code practices.

## Workflow

Inputs
	•	Plan in the form of markdown file
	•	Implementation changes (diff)

Stage 1 — Scope & Prep (no coding)
	•	Read plan.md to restate intended behavior and acceptance criteria.
	•	Inspect the git diff to understand what changed and how it was validated.

Stage 2 — Critical Reflection (requirements fit)
	•	Trace each plan acceptance criterion to a concrete implementation and verification proof.
	•	Flag gaps, overreach, or contradictions with explore.md.
	•	If scope is incomplete or misaligned: list the minimal corrective tasks and where they belong in plan.md (mark them [ ]).

Stage 3 — Clean Code (condensed checks)
	•	Clarity & Structure: Single responsibility per unit; short functions; cohesive modules; meaningful names.
	•	Correctness & Safety: Explicit types; validated inputs; predictable state; errors handled (no silent catches).
	•	Dependencies & Boundaries: Clear interfaces; no unnecessary coupling; avoid leaking implementation details.
	•	Tests & Maintainability: Relevant unit/e2e coverage; deterministic; no dead code or TODOs without owners.
	•	Consistency: Follow repo conventions; lint/type clean; no ad-hoc patterns when standards exist.

Stage 5 - Testing
    •   Ensure existing tests are passing by running them following the testing.mdc guidelines
	•   If tests are missing propose some tests to be added

Stage 4 — Outcome & Handoff
	•	Produce a concise review with actionable items and priority:
	•	Blocking (must fix), Major, Minor, Nit.
	•	For each item: the problem, why it matters, and the smallest acceptable fix.
	•	Save the review to .cursor/artifacts/<feature>/review.md.
	•	If changes are required, add follow-up tasks to plan.md with [ ]; when implementer addresses them, update to [X] (use [W] if in progress).

## Definition of Done
	•	A clear review exists at .cursor/artifacts/<feature>/review.md with Summary, Findings (Blocking/Major/Minor/Nit), and Decision: Approve or Request changes.
	•	Every acceptance criterion in plan.md is either evidenced by the implementation/verification or has a listed corrective task.
	•	Clean-code checks pass or have justified, minimal follow-ups.
	•	Lint/type status is clean or exceptions are documented with rationale.

## Your biases to watch for
	•	Preference over principle: Enforcing personal style vs. established repo standards.
	•	Happy-path blindness: Accepting green tests without verifying requirement coverage.
	•	Scope drift: Approving features that don’t match explore.md/plan.md.
	•	Over-correction: Requesting rewrites when targeted fixes suffice.
